# Environment variables for the weather app (Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed
# vars to the client). Copy to .env and fill in what you have — everything
# here is optional; the app degrades gracefully without it.
#
# SECURITY GUARDRAIL (DAYMARK-SEC-010):
#   Every VITE_* value is PUBLIC. Vite inlines them into the JavaScript
#   bundle that ships to every visitor — never put a private or paid-API
#   key behind VITE_*. If a future integration (e.g. PurpleAir) needs a
#   confidential key, it must go through a small server/edge function,
#   not the client bundle.

# Optional: PurpleAir API key — would enable the nearest-real-sensor PM2.5
# comparison in the "Your micro-climate" card. No code consumes this yet.
# A free READ-ONLY key (https://develop.purpleair.com) is tolerable in the
# bundle because it only spends your quota; if you ever hold a paid key,
# proxy the request server-side instead of using VITE_*.
VITE_PURPLEAIR_API_KEY=
